  (Internal Consistency — values here must match acceleration-report.md,
  Traceability Matrix, and Acceleration Curve).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes the
      twelve tokens above from metrics.json and writes the result into
      acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - Each *_DISPLAY token is a renderer-pre-formatted string. For a
      numeric multiplier (e.g., "1.4") the renderer appends the Unicode
      multiplier sign U+00D7 (MULTIPLICATION SIGN), NOT the ASCII letter
      x (U+0078). For a non-numeric value the renderer substitutes the
      canonical phrase "Insufficient signal — <reason>" verbatim with
      NO trailing × — an unmeasurable metric never renders as
      "Insufficient signal — <reason>×". The "Insufficient signal"
      phrasing is canonical per AAP §0.7.2.1 and MUST NOT be replaced
      by alternative wordings such as "unavailable" or "missing".
    - Each *_CAVEAT token expands to the canonical caveat string from
      metrics.json. For a Low or Insufficient-signal metric the caveat
      explains the underlying boundary condition (per AAP §0.7.2.2
      Rule 3 — every Low / Insufficient metric MUST carry an explicit
      caveat). When a metric is High-confidence with no caveat to
      surface, the renderer substitutes the empty string and the
      .kpi-caveat element renders blank.
    - Each *_CONF token expands to the CSS class suffix
      ("high" | "medium" | "low"), so the rendered span becomes
      <span class="confidence-low">Low</span>. The confidence badge
      styles are defined in acceleration/templates/deck/theme.css
      (.confidence-high / .confidence-medium / .confidence-low).
    - Per AAP §0.2.3 baseline state, Metric 9 is expected to render at
      Low confidence with the canonical "Insufficient signal — GitHub
      Releases API not accessible" phrase when no GITHUB_TOKEN is
      present, and Metric 11 at Low confidence with "Insufficient
      signal — CI test history unavailable" when Actions artifacts
      cannot be downloaded. Metric 8 is rendered from the data source
      actually used at runtime (issue-tracker incident labels → High;
      revert-attribution proxy → Medium; otherwise Insufficient signal).
    - The kpi-grid uses CSS auto-fit (theme.css line 268-273), so three
      cards on a 1920×1080 slide render side-by-side with min-width
      280px and 1.5em gap.
    - The renderer is the single source of truth (metrics.json); the
      multipliers shown here MUST be identical to the values reported
      in acceleration-report.md (Rule 4 — Internal Consistency,
      verified by verify_report.py).
    - Tone discipline (Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral): "Delivery & Stability"
      is the canonical DORA-adjacent framing. The sublabels reference
      the metric number and a short factual descriptor. The forbidden
      subjective-qualifier list in the Boundaries directive does not
      appear in the visible slide body.
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">DORA-Adjacent</span>
  <h3>Delivery &amp; Stability (8, 9, 11)</h3>
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Problem Records</span>
      <div class="{{M8_VALUE_CLASS}}">{{M8_SHORT}}</div>
      <span class="kpi-sublabel">Metric 8 · Production incidents</span>
      <span class="confidence-{{M8_CONF}}">{{M8_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
      <span class="kpi-caveat">{{M8_CAVEAT}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Releases</span>
      <div class="{{M9_VALUE_CLASS}}">{{M9_SHORT}}</div>
      <span class="kpi-sublabel">Metric 9 · GitHub Releases per phase</span>
      <span class="confidence-{{M9_CONF}}">{{M9_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
      <span class="kpi-caveat">{{M9_CAVEAT}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Escaped Defects</span>
      <div class="{{M11_VALUE_CLASS}}">{{M11_SHORT}}</div>
      <span class="kpi-sublabel">Metric 11 · Test regressions on main</span>
      <span class="confidence-{{M11_CONF}}">{{M11_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
      <span class="kpi-caveat">{{M11_CAVEAT}}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
